WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:02.895
Welcome to SysNDD.

00:03.029 --> 00:05.641
Let's find the evidence for a gene.

00:06.133 --> 00:11.475
Where is the evidence for a gene,
and have you found all of it?

00:11.609 --> 00:14.416
We follow <i>TBL1XR1</i> through four places:

00:14.549 --> 00:20.134
SysNDD, the curated summaries, PubMed, and preprints.

00:20.633 --> 00:24.443
Start in SysNDD and open the gene page.

00:24.576 --> 00:27.366
Under Associated, <i>TBL1XR1</i> has two entities:

00:27.500 --> 00:31.503
an intellectual developmental disorder,

00:31.636 --> 00:33.251
and Pierpont syndrome.

00:33.384 --> 00:36.875
Each entity needs its own assessment.

00:37.367 --> 00:41.263
Then open an entity and read its dates.

00:41.397 --> 00:45.788
This one was last updated in August 2026,

00:45.922 --> 00:49.740
when its category moved from Limited to Definitive.

00:49.873 --> 00:54.652
Its clinical synopsis was last reviewed in 2014,

00:54.785 --> 00:58.423
so check which papers appeared since then.

00:58.933 --> 01:05.239
OMIM, Online Mendelian Inheritance in Man,
links two disorders to the gene,

01:05.373 --> 01:07.306
each with its own number.

01:07.440 --> 01:11.052
That number usually becomes the disease of the entity.

01:11.185 --> 01:14.040
GeneReviews has no chapter for this gene,

01:14.173 --> 01:17.205
so the primary papers carry the evidence.

01:17.338 --> 01:23.574
If a chapter exists,
note its PubMed identifier, the PMID.

01:24.067 --> 01:26.893
For PubMed, first collect the gene's names.

01:27.026 --> 01:34.026
HGNC, the HUGO Gene Nomenclature Committee,
lists the aliases of <i>TBL1XR1</i>.

01:34.768 --> 01:39.999
One of them is <i>TBLR1</i>,
and some papers use only that name.

01:40.500 --> 01:44.287
In PubMed, tag each name with tiab,
for title and abstract.

01:44.421 --> 01:49.564
This keeps the search to papers about the gene.

01:49.697 --> 01:55.307
Join the alias with OR,
and then add the disorder: intellectual disability,

01:55.440 --> 01:58.340
developmental delay or autism.

01:58.833 --> 02:02.532
Look for case reports, case series and cohorts.

02:02.665 --> 02:06.726
This 2023 series adds four new cases.

02:06.859 --> 02:12.708
It reviews 47 individuals reported before,
and pools all 51.

02:12.841 --> 02:16.332
You may have counted some of those 47 already.

02:16.465 --> 02:20.801
Match patients by variant, sex, age and family.

02:20.935 --> 02:25.046
Count each individual and each family once.

02:25.533 --> 02:27.953
Preprints often come first.

02:28.087 --> 02:33.701
This bioRxiv preprint from May 2025
has functional data on <i>TBLR1</i>.

02:33.835 --> 02:40.835
Its page says Now published
in Nature Communications, with a link.

02:41.567 --> 02:46.811
Follow the link and work from the published version.

02:46.944 --> 02:51.228
Cite its PMID and read the final text,
because details can change.

02:51.361 --> 02:55.858
Before publication, a preprint
can be considered individually:

02:55.991 --> 02:58.687
enter its digital object identifier,

02:58.821 --> 03:02.286
the DOI, in the comment field.

03:02.767 --> 03:07.939
Remember: start in SysNDD and
read every entity with its dates.

03:08.072 --> 03:10.771
Search with tiab and the HGNC aliases,

03:10.904 --> 03:15.565
and count each individual and each family once.

03:15.698 --> 03:19.486
And check whether each preprint is now published.

03:19.967 --> 03:23.689
Each step is in the SysNDD documentation.

03:23.822 --> 03:27.967
In video B3, we read one paper for curation.
